 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 464,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "A high blood pressure (BP) reading: is it really HYPERTENSION, and is there a CAUSE?",
   "lines": [
    "ONE high reading is not hypertension, and not an emergency on its own · measure properly: seated, back supported, feet flat, arm at heart level, 5 min rest, 2–3 readings · never on an exam table or hospital bed",
    "then estimate cardiovascular RISK (Framingham) and treat: see the HYPERTENSION TREATMENT chart"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_dx",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 440,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "1 · Is it HYPERTENSION?",
   "lines": [
    "visit 1: history, exam, tests"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_cx",
   "x": 525,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 1118,
   "h": 60,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "2 · Is there a CAUSE? Most have none: PRIMARY (essential) hypertension",
   "lines": [
    "EVERY patient: urinalysis · K+, Na+, creatinine · Ca2+ + albumin · TSH · HbA1c · lipids · 12-lead ECG"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "t_v1",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 256,
   "w": 440,
   "h": 96,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "Visit 1 reading",
   "lines": [
    "• ≥ 180/110 → HYPERTENSION now",
    "• automated office (AOBP) < 135/85 or office < 140/90 → none: recheck yearly"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "oo_head_0_0",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 432,
   "w": 214,
   "h": 98,
   "kind": "oo_h",
   "title": "OUT of office: ambulatory (ABPM) or home (HBPM)",
   "lines": [
    "ABPM is the gold standard: NIGHT readings predict risk best"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "of_head_0_0",
   "x": 271,
   "y": 432,
   "w": 214,
   "h": 98,
   "kind": "of_h",
   "title": "OFFICE readings only",
   "lines": [
    "the alternative: more visits"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "dr_head_0_0",
   "x": 525,
   "y": 432,
   "w": 214,
   "h": 98,
   "kind": "dr_h",
   "title": "Habits and DRUGS",
   "lines": [
    "self- or doctor-inflicted"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "os_head_0_0",
   "x": 751,
   "y": 432,
   "w": 214,
   "h": 98,
   "kind": "os_h",
   "title": "Obstructive sleep apnea (OSA)",
   "lines": [
    "the commonest secondary cause"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "pa_head_0_0",
   "x": 977,
   "y": 432,
   "w": 214,
   "h": 98,
   "kind": "pa_h",
   "title": "Primary aldosteronism",
   "lines": []
  },
  {
